# Cline project rules — security-posture-platform

## Repo layout
- Backend API: `services/api/` (Python, FastAPI; settings in `services/api/app/settings.py`)
- Frontend: `services/frontend/` (Next.js App Router under `services/frontend/app/`, components in `services/frontend/components/`)
- Infra/K8s: `infra/`, Helm + manifests under `artifacts/`
- This is a SECURITY product. Be careful with anything touching secrets, auth, or data flow.

## Working style
- This is a large repo (~672 files, 6k+ symbols). Don't bulk-read files — open only what a task needs.
- Scope edits to the named feature's file (e.g. the findings page = `services/frontend/app/(app)/findings/page.tsx`).
- Routine UI work (CSS/Tailwind, copy, simple components) keep changes minimal and in-style.
- Match surrounding code: naming, comment density, idioms.

## Guardrails
- Don't commit or push unless asked.
- Before deleting/overwriting a file, inspect it first.
- Flag any change that touches authentication, secret handling, or external data egress.

## Quality gates
- After every edit, re-read the file to verify the diff applied correctly — don't trust edit output alone.
- For scripts (PowerShell, bash, Python), trace all data paths end-to-end: where does each variable come from, where does it go, does it cross a container/host boundary incorrectly.
- If you haven't tested a change, say so explicitly. Never claim a script works if it hasn't been executed.
- If the shell is broken or output truncated, find another way to verify (read lock files, search for installed binaries, check file timestamps).
- When creating new files, verify they exist with a read after creation.
- PowerShell-specific: check `-or` vs null-coalesce, container-vs-host path confusion in volume mounts, deprecated image registries (Docker Hub → GHCR moves), and that ZAP risk codes only go 0–3 (no "Critical").
